                    <signifLet xml:id="m-6c08e1ac-5d61-428a-b807-ddaaaaf0b65f" /></nc><nc xml:id="m-6474cda1-fbf6-4acc-9a0d-b3ee47e7622f" pname="a" oct="3" /></neume></syllable><divLine xml:id="m-b86674d9-6ab0-42dc-9fbe-07ed256b4a68" facs="#m-50bcbb9e-b448-4a85-a4f6-20b1fc811c1c" form="finalis" /></layer></staff><div xml:id="m-29b65922-da2e-430b-bcb6-4067103ef52a">
            <lg xml:id="m-75b9738c-d3ab-46aa-9858-d2e16cd198e1">
              <l xml:id="m-b56f3131-558f-449b-bd30-940efa091444" facs="#m-533d0eb7-3f04-4256-9c60-2a64ee58079e" label="ambiguous">February II.</l><l xml:id="m-4ba4a038-4b5c-43bd-ac4c-76176313491f" facs="#m-21e84aba-2e6b-4d55-a900-0458b5fee2f2" label="ambiguous">1378</l><l xml:id="m-ab06d68f-8904-445f-96cc-6b97a7e82b3a" facs="#m-d04c4293-0644-4359-88b1-8233ee58bc4b" label="text-like">11. The Apparition of Our Blessed Lady at Lourdes.</l><l xml:id="m-cf823853-a77d-4419-af93-1099a1bc8af8" facs="#m-2b46e608-045e-4513-9c79-fc2ef471c9fc" label="ambiguous">Double major.</l><l xml:id="m-0294f93b-e435-41dc-889c-d948df98eaa6" facs="#m-9a8bb723-48d8-4dfa-a8a7-a8ff7694ac16" label="text-like">AT FIRST VESPERS.</l><l xml:id="m-f85c6675-45b2-484c-95c2-c80fc0979363" facs="#m-763c3ef5-f83d-4708-8221-3639ec5a41ff" label="text-like">All as at second Vespers, p. 1880, except the following:</l><l xml:id="m-916a6cd7-e988-4797-8cbc-8ae74e4bde2c" facs="#m-ed2c998d-a564-40b9-99ae-d232c19a8cf7" label="lyrics-like">Hymn. Ave máris stélla. p. 1259. However, if the second Vesper¬ &amp;</l><l xml:id="m-872722df-cee4-43f7-bc91-5efb219c6397" facs="#m-9cd504e5-458a-4ad4-b56b-cbaa1b7624ac" label="lyrics-like">this feast are not said, the hymn at first Vespers is Omnis expértem. as on</l><l xml:id="m-67be827a-322f-4f19-94c1-4553eb80331b" facs="#m-bd1549c5-c7a4-42b0-b09e-500a4a1ad283" label="ambiguous">.1582.</l><l xml:id="m-9ed8c88e-a64e-4a52-9407-4cd4c3034863" facs="#m-8a0df73f-489d-4699-bf4d-7f9d75cf2a7e" label="lyrics-like">V. Dignáre me laudáre te, Virgo sacráta.</l><l xml:id="m-4b7ec7ea-d5a0-402d-a75e-e8c2ca79c814" facs="#m-42e661ed-9139-4b4c-ad69-753b2202ec27" label="lyrics-like">R. Da mihi virtútem contra hóstes túos.</l><l xml:id="m-f53c428a-1cea-4c06-ac27-b5e62425569c" facs="#m-8ee4890f-af01-4152-9de1-2a0f62d1aece" label="text-like">At Magn.</l><l xml:id="m-dd33b621-8217-4505-8d82-89575031fe56" facs="#m-bf75958f-696d-4571-afdb-81cfb448e1bd" label="ambiguous">Ant. 3. a</l><l xml:id="m-b63e9d24-e620-4162-a662-c688e0a03b3e" facs="#m-c75aafff-ddba-4b6a-984e-3ff8cf21f45f" label="ambiguous">1</l><l xml:id="m-08e71004-b99d-4009-8849-4a0f8e524096" facs="#m-dfca6305-90e2-41e9-987a-db6d703c2d58" label="lyrics-like">-sta est * co-lúmba mé-a</l><l xml:id="m-ed585303-6925-4672-95f5-14c47eeffe3b" facs="#m-14b96966-9c3b-4e36-89b8-41ebc0933375" label="lyrics-like">perfécta mé-a,</l><l xml:id="m-ce2febf7-31c5-4b62-b1e5-d9dcbe0f4ada" facs="#m-52f3849f-8e8e-4d2f-bf8d-baac69e8d700" label="lyrics-like">immacu-lá-ta mé- a. E u o u a e.</l><l xml:id="m-2c44c02b-56d4-4750-8e32-378c34c58da5" facs="#m-da9d4011-66b1-451b-8e09-d5ec3b89a4ab" label="lyrics-like">Cant. Magníficat. 3. a. p. 208.</l><l xml:id="m-5df8c287-9dc9-4102-a783-e01db971d036" facs="#m-216437ae-878b-40c7-ae60-64510df5b129" label="lyrics-like">Prayer. Deus, qui per Immaculátam. D. 1376.</l><l xml:id="m-e6d2ffa3-a10f-49cf-b8af-86af603189f1" facs="#m-2747a470-14e6-4878-b057-ea4fd31613ad" label="text-like">For the Hymn of Compline and of the Little Hours the chant and</l><l xml:id="m-aeb88809-9ef6-4d60-bb37-6c3deeea66ab" facs="#m-1262c2db-6993-43f8-bdf2-0fa953bb742f" label="text-like">doxolosy are as on feasts or the Blessed Virgin, p. 268.</l><l xml:id="m-0579f1a9-dc4e-41b3-9b22-90c0591514f8" facs="#m-6e2396f4-5198-49ed-9494-01da80ce052d" label="lyrics-like">At Prime. Ant. Cándor est. D. 1380. In the Short Resp., the Y. 1s Qui</l><l xml:id="m-958a018e-da6f-4133-ac79-61955bec349d" facs="#m-d1cff3d9-67c0-4932-b3ab-87ca9b4e6190" label="lyrics-like">nátus es. Short Lesson. In me grátia. p. 1380.</l><l xml:id="m-8e94f7a6-7ebe-4e8a-9090-26374bb349c7" facs="#m-df8c3de1-9540-4901-bdaf-de426bf6a9a4" label="text-like">AT TERCE.</l><l xml:id="m-fd31d202-ec7a-4ee0-aaa6-4fda18448bc3" facs="#m-26f19efe-1b99-4a81-a533-78ea2a30a595" label="lyrics-like">Hymn. p. 1256. Ant. Múlier. p. 1380. Chapter of Vespers, Surge. D. 1381.</l><l xml:id="m-f51a02eb-9284-431f-b05d-cc6e835ac04a" facs="#m-ed76b464-bcd9-4be9-91d8-8f93e7712541" label="ambiguous">short !</l><l xml:id="m-5db74a16-6180-496c-9411-0f5b18d79fcc" facs="#m-5d830617-2a06-4616-9d57-191ef6d23f4c" label="ambiguous">Resp.</l><l xml:id="m-6f522a74-3c19-433c-8103-d4064c0e07a5" facs="#m-0dfc0a7b-a565-475a-a1d8-752d2c9cd11a" label="lyrics-like">Uae est ísta quae ascéndit de desérto, “Delí-ci-is</l><l xml:id="m-71cf584c-4207-460f-80bf-5b265a5634d6" facs="#m-6defbdce-117f-4ad4-bd6a-65fb521f05d8" label="lyrics-like">áfflu-ens? V. Inníxa super di-léctum sú-um. Gló-ri-a</l><l xml:id="m-bee2e19f-89ff-4a3f-9906-bede0466adfd" facs="#m-7139ab4d-4d33-4d21-87dc-c8088fce784b" label="lyrics-like">Pátri, et Fí-li-o, et Spi-rí-tu-i Sáncto.</l><l xml:id="m-ae12e694-ac5f-4910-be56-35bbc2aead10" facs="#m-2117ebf6-a57d-4200-801a-c49ff1fc743c" label="lyrics-like">x. Vidérunt éam filiae Sion.</l><l xml:id="m-a21961d9-0f51-492a-a5b3-1a062083af1d" facs="#m-5b6714be-8778-4417-978f-b34a731b5ee0" label="lyrics-like">R. Et beatíssimam praedicavérunt.</l></lg></div></section></score></mdiv></body></music>
</mei>